Community. ;)

Perhaps that’s how meaning survives beyond any individual carrier.

Not merely through preservation, but through participation, transmission, correction, and renewal.

A community can remember what an individual forgets, adapt what an institution freezes, and rediscover meaning that language has lost.

And the interesting part is that community isn’t just the collection of its members. It’s also the relationships between them, the shared practices, and the things they create together.

Code can rot. Institutions can decay. Individuals come and go.

But a living community can repair, reinterpret, and regenerate.

Continuity without requiring permanence.

And there’s the reciprocal: communities can also preserve errors, amplify distortions, and resist necessary change.

So perhaps the real measure of a healthy community isn’t simply what it remembers.

It’s what it can learn, unlearn, and rebuild together.